    "problem_statement": "List variable assignment produces reversed strings when no match groups present\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen using List variables in TextFSM templates, if the regex pattern doesn't contain any match groups, the assigned values are being reversed (string is reversed character by character).\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport textfsm\n\n# Template with List variable but no match groups in regex\ntemplate_text = \"\"\"\nValue List ITEMS (.+)\n\nStart\n  ^${ITEMS} -> Record\n\"\"\"\n\n# Input data\ndata = \"\"\"\nitem1\nitem2\nitem3\n\"\"\"\n\ntemplate = textfsm.TextFSM(io.StringIO(template_text))\nresults = template.ParseText(data)\nprint(\"Results:\", results)\n# Expected: [['item1', 'item2', 'item3']]\n# Actual: [['1meti', '2meti', '3meti']]\n```\n\nThe issue occurs when a List variable's regex pattern has no capture groups - instead of storing the matched string as-is, it gets reversed before being added to the list."
